{"abstract":"One of the most important tests available to assess human vision is the visual field test, or perimetry. While imaging of the fundus and standard tests such as Snellen charts can assess factors such as acuity, and identify damaged parts of the retina, only the visual field test can measure the subjective field of view of perception from the patient side. We introduce a Virtual Reality (VR)-based perimetry test. A systematic test for measuring the visual field function conducted in VR. The VR-based test is precise enough to supersede the standard perimetry test carried out on either a Goldmann or Octopus test machine. Using VR allows for a more comfortable experience and opens up for further development that can potentially be used to map out other deficiencies of the visual field function. It also provides the ability to gamify the test allowing it to be carried out on children. Here we present some of the considerations and implementation details which ensure that our software has the necessary capabilities of producing correct measurements and valid results.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Gasior, Kacper Bej","Jensen, Mark Bo","Maare, Jonas Ulveman","Doherty, Kevin","Mulvey, Fiona Bríd"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-788726"],"event":{"end":"2024-08-31","place":"Dublin, ie","start":"2024-08-30","title":"ACM Symposium on Applied Perception 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Ireland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University College Dublin"],"keyword":["Mixed reality","Virtual reality","Vision loss","Visual field"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"virtual reality the future of visual field testing","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85205090775","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-788726","identifier":[{"id":"85205090775","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-142ae6be-46b4-49ce-a480-cc6f5202654b"],"keyword":["Mixed reality","Perimetry test","Virtual reality","Vision loss","Visual field"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-00F093583D40CA03FC6860BCF1708360"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ie","key":"university college dublin","loc":["Ireland","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University College Dublin","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kacper Bej","key":"gasiorpau","last":"Gasior","locid":"e9199148-59ef-46c1-b028-44885cbf377a","name":"Gasior, Kacper Bej","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mark Bo","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"1491df9a-478c-4e02-b3e5-5d529b4cb9af","name":"Jensen, Mark Bo","orcid":"0000-0002-2387-1568","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas Ulveman","key":"maarepau","last":"Maare","name":"Maare, Jonas Ulveman","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kevin","key":"dohertypau","last":"Doherty","name":"Doherty, Kevin","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Fiona Bríd","key":"mulveypau","last":"Mulvey","locid":"6f5a2134-46e1-430e-865b-4b0c7a10c08b","name":"Mulvey, Fiona Bríd","orcid":"0000-0001-6422-6592","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":