{"abstract":"We present a working paper on integrating eye tracking with mixed and augmented reality for the benefit of low vision aids. We outline the current state of the art and relevant research and point to further research and development required in order to adapt to individual user, environment, and current task. We outline key technical challenges and possible solutions including calibration, dealing with variant eye data quality, measuring and adapting image processing to low vision within current technical limitations, and outline an experimental approach to designing data-driven solutions using machine learning and artificial intelligence.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Mulvey, Fiona Bríd","Mikitovic, Marek","Sadowski, Mateusz","Hou, Baosheng James","Rasamoel, Nils David","Hansen, John Paulin","Bækgaard, Per"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-327402"],"event":{"end":"2021-05-27","place":"Virtual event","start":"2021-05-25","title":"13th ACM Symposium on Eye Tracking Research and Applications","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Mulvey, Fiona Bríd"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"gaze interactive and attention aware low vision aids as future smart glasses","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3450341.3460769","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-327402","identifier":[{"id":"85107973473","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-4cb5e1f9-0e0d-4565-9b97-68d5699296cf"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6876D742A2F09051D8938A9E0968CF55"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3450341.3460769","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/254760951/3450341.3460769.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Cognitive Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Fiona Bríd","key":"mulveypau","last":"Mulvey","locid":"6f5a2134-46e1-430e-865b-4b0c7a10c08b","name":"Mulvey, Fiona Bríd","orcid":"0000-0001-6422-6592","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marek","key":"mikitovicpau","last":"Mikitovic","name":"Mikitovic, Marek","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mateusz","key":"sadowskipau","last":"Sadowski","name":"Sadowski, Mateusz","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Baosheng","key":"houpau","last":"Hou","locid":"cf491a19-a640-4cee-a664-87853b1c5531","name":"Hou, Baosheng James","name_org":"Hou, Baosheng","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nils David","key":"rasamoelpau","last":"Rasamoel","locid":"058a3521-e1bc-449f-b162-4838559337af","name":"Rasamoel, Nils David","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"John Paulin","key":"paulinhansenpau","last":"Paulin Hansen","locid":"119e0e25-cbb9-478c-bee2-db6d2d9c4b90","name":"Hansen, John Paulin","name_org":"Paulin Hansen, John Paulin","orcid":"0000-0001-5594-3645","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Per","key":"bækgaardpau","last":"Bækgaard","locid":"c7b6e25e-b81b-402f-81c1-7e6ef56e2334","name":"Bækgaard, Per","orcid":"0000-0002-6720-1128","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3450341.3460769","publisher":"ACM","status":"p","title":"Eye Tracking Research and Applications Symposium","volume":"169260"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85107973473"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-4cb5e1f9-0e0d-4565-9b97-68d5699296cf"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Gaze Interactive and Attention Aware Low Vision Aids as Future Smart Glasses","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-327402","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"The aim of this research is to investigate the explication of levels of attention through eye movement parameters. Previous research from disparate fields have suggested that eye movements are related to cognitive processing, however, the exact nature of the relationship is unclear. Since eye movements can be controlled either by bottom up stimulus properties or by top down cognitive control, studies have compared eye movements in real world tasks and searched for indicators of cognitive load or level of attention when task demands increase. Extracting the effects of cognitive processing on eye movements from the effect of the changing nature of the stimulus is difficult. Characterising and confirming the parameters of levels of processing in eye movements requires measures with the explicit intention of systematically varying task demands while also taking account of individual differences. This series of studies attempts to provide explanatory information for previous findings that saccade amplitude and fixation duration are indicative of levels of processing and to isolate top down influences on eye movements with a stimulus driven approach. This approach involves developing measures suitable for studying individual differences in attention in large sample groups, using stimulus pairs which are similar in terms of bottom up properties but different in terms of higher level processing. These methods are presented in study 1, stimuli are developed and tested in Study 2. Study 3 uses these stimuli to investigate individual differences in levels of processing within the normal population using existing constructs and tests of cognitive style. Study 4 investigates these stimuli and the eye movements of a clinical group with known interruption to the dorsal stream of processing, and subsequent isolated difficulty with certain aspects of visual cognition. Results are presented in terms of the development of methods for assessing and tracking individual differences in cognition and subjective attentional states in real time through eye movement analysis.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Mulvey, Fiona Bríd"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383184"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"levels of processing and eye movements a stimulus driven approach","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"do","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-383184","ids":["itu-824c8334-480a-43aa-aa55-80cecba06d14"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-A1CEFFB2A3CA32CB999247DBD0E625C1"],"org":[{"affno":1,"key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU"}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Fiona Bríd","key":"mulveypau","last":"Mulvey","locid":"0e2c06ee-d065-4477-93e1-d5ccf2f48fec","name":"Mulvey, Fiona Bríd","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-824c8334-480a-43aa-aa55-80cecba06d14"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Levels of processing and Eye Movements: A Stimulus driven approach","type":"Other","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383184","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"author_count":3,"contributors":["Mulvey, Fiona Bríd","Perrone, Gian David","Holmquist, Kenneth"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381471"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lund University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a novel interpolation based method for the extraction of velocity profiles from low medium and high frequency eye data","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.jemr.org/online/4/3/1","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381471","ids":["itu-0dd08723-a60e-4259-a375-bb57fc3a962b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-08F8DF65AF7B2235E0169136C49E958C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.jemr.org/online/4/3/1","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["The Department, Theoretical Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Fiona Bríd","key":"mulveypau","last":"Mulvey","locid":"0e2c06ee-d065-4477-93e1-d5ccf2f48fec","name":"Mulvey, Fiona Bríd","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Gian David","key":"perronepau","last":"Perrone","name":"Perrone, Gian David","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kenneth","key":"holmquistpau","last":"Holmquist","name":"Holmquist, Kenneth","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["19333196","1933320X"],"issn_org":["19958692"],"issue":"3","journal":"Journal of EMDR Practice and Research","pages":"203-203","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Journal of EMDR Practice and Research","title_org":"Journal of Eye Movement and Research","volume":"4"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-0dd08723-a60e-4259-a375-bb57fc3a962b"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A novel interpolation based method for the extraction of velocity profiles from low, medium and high frequency eye data","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381471","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"This paper introduces the concept of using gaze as a sole modality for fully controlling player characters of fast-paced action computer games. A user experiment is devised to collect gaze and gameplay data from subjects playing a version of the popular Super Mario Bros platform game. The initial analysis shows that there is a rather limited grid around Mario where the efficient player focuses her attention the most while playing the game. The useful grid as we name it, projects the amount of meaningful visual information a designer should use towards creating successful player character controllers with the use of artificial intelligence for a platform game like Super Mario. Information about the eyes' position on the screen and the state of the game are utilized as inputs of an artificial neural network, which is trained to approximate which keyboard action is to be performed at each game step. Results yield a prediction accuracy of over 83% on unseen data samples and show promise towards the development of eye-controlled fast-paced platform games. Derived neural network players are intended to be used as assistive technology tools for the digital entertainment of people with motor disabilities.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Muñoz, Jorge","Yannakakis, Georgios N.","Mulvey, Fiona Bríd","Hansen, Dan Witzner","Gutierrez, German","Sanchis, Araceli"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382361"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Game AI"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"towards gaze controlled platform games","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/CIG.2011.6031988","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382361","identifier":[{"id":"80054013729","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-494d4082-cae2-48c3-a993-7381c219cc28"],"keyword":["game ai"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2BB015CAA2810C88EB8802FBA3233F66"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/CIG.2011.6031988","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Play","The Department, Computer Games and Interaction Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jorge","key":"muñozpau","last":"Muñoz","name":"Muñoz, Jorge","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Georgios N.","key":"yannakakispau","last":"Yannakakis","name":"Yannakakis, Georgios N.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Fiona","key":"mulveypau","last":"Mulvey","locid":"0e2c06ee-d065-4477-93e1-d5ccf2f48fec","name":"Mulvey, Fiona Bríd","name_org":"Mulvey, Fiona","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dan Witzner","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"5ad9c220-e37f-443a-8a31-fc4abf365db5","name":"Hansen, Dan Witzner","orcid":"0000-0002-6780-4471","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"German","key":"gutierrezpau","last":"Gutierrez","name":"Gutierrez, German","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Araceli","key":"sanchispau","last":"Sanchis","name":"Sanchis, Araceli","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/cig.2011.6031988","isbn":["9781457700095"],"pages":"47-54","status":"p","title":"Computational Intelligence and Games (CIG), 2011 IEEE Conference on"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-80054013729"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-494d4082-cae2-48c3-a993-7381c219cc28"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Towards gaze-controlled platform games","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382361","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Eye and gaze tracking have a long history but there is still plenty of room for further development. In this concluding chapter for Section 6, we consider future perspectives for the development of eye and gaze tracking.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Hansen, Dan Witzner","Mulvey, Fiona Bríd","Mardanbegi, Diako"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384042"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Eye tracking","Future Development","Methods"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"discussion and future directions for eye tracker development","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84898560179","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384042","identifier":[{"id":"84898560179","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-bdb10dd0-6a4a-49f8-bc24-b1c9ccb44449"],"keyword":["eye tracking","future development","methods"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-DD13CA5B5DCCEA139ED318724FD3426F"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dan Witzner","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"5ad9c220-e37f-443a-8a31-fc4abf365db5","name":"Hansen, Dan Witzner","orcid":"0000-0002-6780-4471","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Fiona","key":"mulveypau","last":"Mulvey","locid":"0e2c06ee-d065-4477-93e1-d5ccf2f48fec","name":"Mulvey, Fiona Bríd","name_org":"Mulvey, Fiona","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Diako","key":"mardanbegipau","last":"Mardanbegi","name":"Mardanbegi, Diako","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"359-363","status":"p","title":"Discussion and Future Directions for Eye Tracker Development"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-bdb10dd0-6a4a-49f8-bc24-b1c9ccb44449"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Discussion and Future Directions for Eye Tracker Development","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384042","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
